{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Converts Stripe errors into the appropriate Apple Pay error, for use in ","type":"text"},{"code":"PKPaymentAuthorizationResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If the error can be fixed by the customer within the Apple Pay sheet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@objc"},{"kind":"text","text":"(pkPaymentErrorForStripeError:) "},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pkPaymentError","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"forStripeError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stripeError","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"stripeError","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An error from the Stripe SDK."}],"type":"paragraph